# A copy of an Omen spell is an Omen too (CR 720.3c): it has Charring Bite's characteristics, a sorcery, so Lutri's
# "copy target instant or sorcery spell you control" can take the Omen on the stack at all (CR 720.3b). Bot1 casts
# Charring Bite at Bot2's first Llanowar Elves and flashes in Lutri, whose trigger copies it; the copy is aimed at the
# second Elves. Both resolve, killing both Elves. The copy is "shuffled into its owner's library" too, but a copy of a spell
# is no card and ceases to exist out of the stack (CR 707.10a, 704.5e; the ruling: "the copy ceases to exist as a
# state-based action"), so only the card itself joins Bot1's library: eight cards, not nine, and nothing of Bot1's is in
# a graveyard or exile.

